# S03: Guest Identity, Loyalty Ledger and Idempotent Referral

> *«Азиз, тебя с такими инновациями местная молодёжь обанкротит. Ты что не в курсе, как с помощью
> яйца эти утырки штамп перекатывают?»* — the paper punch-card is forgeable. The digital,
> check-summed, server-generated card is not.

## Objective

Give a walk-in guest a stable, scannable, typo-proof identity that is **not** an auth account.
Recompute loyalty from an append-only ledger inside a database trigger rather than in application
code. Prove exactly-once, attribute-isolated referral attribution on the S02 idempotency helper.

## Why this sprint is first

P1 has zero upstream dependencies; P2/P3/P4 all consume it. Today `orders.customer_id` is
`null` for every staff-created and walk-in order (`orders.post.ts:122`,
`create-empty.post.ts:101`), so *no* retention metric is computable until a guest exists.
`profiles` is hard-bound 1:1 to `auth.users` — a walk-in cannot be represented at all, and
deleting the auth user cascades away the entire history.

