## Article traceability

| Article beat | Delivered by |
| ------------ | ------------ |
| Forgeable paper stamps → digital card | T01, T06 |
| `CARD-135633` typo'd into `CARD-136533` | T06 check character + T09 pre-DB rejection |
| "Positive: likes it spicy, no onion" — the substitute waiter reads the card | T10, T14 |
| 4 purchases → 5, 240 bonuses → 290, regular → discount tier | T02, T04 |
| Phone changes / customer refuses to give it | T01 (`phone` descriptive, never a key) |
| Referred girlfriend inherits "triple jalapeño" and screams | T05, T12 (attribute isolation) |

## Definition of Done

- [ ] A walk-in guest with no auth account can be created, given a printable card code, attached
      to an order, and read back by a *different* staff member
- [ ] Marking the same order paid twice awards points exactly once; `points_balance` equals the
      sum of the ledger
- [ ] Redeeming the same referral code twice yields one referral row; a referral that would
      inherit the referrer's preferences is rejected **by the database**
- [ ] A mistyped card code is rejected by the check character before any DB lookup
- [ ] Profile and guest card display the same loyalty tier (two competing truths eliminated)
- [ ] Every guest-PII route rejects a forged `body.userRole` with 403
- [ ] Migrations 031-035 apply idempotently twice; `/api/health/schema` lists the new objects
- [ ] **Owner-visible deliverable:** `/guests` page — search a guest, read their card

## Invariants Produced

1. `public.guests` is the customer of record; `public.profiles` is staff-and-account identity
   only. **No sixth role was created** — the 5-role invariant holds.
2. A card code is server-generated, carries a mod-97 check character, and is never accepted from
   a client.
3. `phone` is descriptive data, never a key and never uniquely constrained.
4. All loyalty mutation happens inside `recompute_loyalty_on_payment()` or through
   `/api/loyalty/adjust` with a caller-supplied `idempotencyKey`. No route writes points directly.
5. `loyalty_accounts.tier` is the only loyalty truth. Deriving a tier from account age is
   prohibited.
6. `orders.guest_id` is the guest linkage; `orders.customer_id` remains the auth linkage. The two
   are maintained independently.
7. A guest may be referred at most once, ever, enforced by `idx_referrals_referred_once`, and
   never inherits referrer attributes.
8. Migration numbering continues at **036**.

## Risk

QR/barcode decoding has **no** library in the locked module set and `BarcodeDetector` is
Chromium-only. T15 must ship the manual-entry fallback regardless; the check character is what
makes that fallback safe. A polyfill dependency is an open question for the user.
